From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Rui Figueira <rfigueira@cloudflare.com>
Date: Sat, 1 Aug 2026 20:35:52 +0100
Subject: [PATCH] Paint re-anchored abspos boxes at their DOM position

"Anchor absolute boxes to their CSS containing block" re-parents an
abspos child of an unpositioned parent onto its containing block so
taffy resolves the insets against the right box. That move also took
the box with it in the paint tree, because paint_children is built from
layout_children: so the box painted after the entire intervening
subtree instead of at its place in DOM order.

CSS 2.1 Appendix E paints a stacking context's z-index:auto positioned
boxes in tree order, so a positioned sibling that comes later in the DOM
must paint on top. todomvc is the everyday casualty: .filters is
abspos with left/right/bottom set and .footer is static, so .filters
re-anchors to .todoapp, paints over the whole footer and swallows every
click on the later .clear-completed button; "Clear completed" did
nothing on the react, preact, vue and angular builds alike.

Split the two concerns: layout keeps the containing-block anchor; paint
and hit-testing re-home the box to the flow parent it was skimmed out
of (paint_parent_override), with rehomed_paint_translate correcting the
origin from containing-block space back into the flow parent's.
Ordering within the merged list uses document order explicitly rather
than leaning on sort stability, which no longer holds once re-homed
boxes are appended.

Two boundaries the re-home must respect:

 - z-index auto/0 boxes only. A z-indexed box is hoisted into its
   stacking context by flush_styles_to_layout, with coordinates unwound
   up the layout recursion; re-homing it feeds that unwind the wrong
   base (the select-dropdown overlay, z-index 2^31-1, painted
   displaced). Its paint order is governed by z-index anyway.

 - taffy's bounds cannot cover a re-homed box (it is not a layout child
   of its flow parent), and both hit-prune and paint-cull trust those
   bounds: a select's overlay extends below the select, and abspos
   under a zero-height <body> is outside it entirely, so hits and
   clipped screenshots dropped them. compute_rehomed_reach, run after
   taffy layout (the one geometry pass in resolve that is never stale),
   unions each host's re-homed boxes and propagates the rect up the
   layout-parent chain; hit-prune and paint-cull widen their bounds by
   that reach. An earlier flag-based variant simply disabled the
   shortcuts along flagged chains; on heavy pages the flag reached
   the root, culling effectively turned off, and the recorded scene
   ballooned until the renderer's wasm aborted mid-screenshot.

Scope is limited to boxes the abspos-anchoring patch already moves: a
page with no re-anchored abspos builds exactly the paint tree it did
before.

Against blitz-dom 0.3.0-beta.3: Taffy now lays out every out-of-flow box
against its CSS containing block natively (so the earlier re-anchoring
patches are not needed) and upstream's paint tree lists such a box under
its containing block, right after the layout child it descends from.
That still paints it above later positioned boxes inside that child, so
the re-home moves to layout/paint_tree.rs: a z-index:auto abspos box
whose containing block is not its flow parent is listed (and hit-tested)
by its flow parent, with rehomed_paint_translate measured from the box's
oof_containing_block. compute_rehomed_reach now runs after the
paint-tree build, which is where re-homes are recorded.
